<urn:beads-cache:finding:C2-REQ-009> triage:qa6Review "{\"owner\": \"background C2 rust-developer, with upstream public compatibility restoration owned by sc-runtime\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-6\", \"reviewed_commit\": \"08f7cee0308f52eb0a5a0067cb4e209e2c82806e\", \"reviewer_records\": [{\"finding\": {\"category\": \"acceptance-gap\", \"compliance_result\": \"partially-compliant\", \"id\": \"C2-REQ-009\", \"issue\": \"The former reserve/free/rebind race is removed in source: released run_with_cleanup_and_bound reports the continuously owned listener and both new fixtures include competing-bind controls plus actual Application cleanup. However all affected cancellation tests currently fail compilation because published SDK0.2 omits testing::instrument_router. Consequently current causal HTTP timeout/BUSY retention, real signal/instance-lock/readiness join/restart and portable cleanup tests have not qualified. Production Windows CtrlBreak registration/polling is present, but the current native Windows job never reaches installed graceful-stop/reap/restart. Service-bound startup251.961ms<500ms and real scratch stop samples are credited without being substituted for these daemon observables.\", \"required_correction\": \"Retain real public runtime endpoint/cleanup/signal/instance ownership and deterministic competing-bind assertions. Consume the approved published optional genuine timeout/tracking wrapper or equivalent public seam; qualify these original50ms HTTP/1s read cancellation cases and supported-platform process lifecycle including Windows CTRL_BREAK/clean exit/physical joins/descendant reap/unlock/restart. No private control, reserve-free-rebind, replacement middleware, retries/sleeps, test exclusion or timeout widening.\", \"severity\": \"Blocking\", \"source_refs\": [\"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-2-framework-application.md:273\", \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-2-framework-application.md:285\", \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-2-framework-application.md:310\", \"docs/bd