ry020-resume/application-clippy.log\"], \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/runtime_lifecycle.rs\", \"id\": \"C2-REQ-009\", \"line\": 106, \"remediation\": \"Consume an approved published restoration of the existing optional public test-util timeout/tracking wrapper, then qualify these actual runtime/application lifecycle paths under all original budgets and supported-platform controls. Preserve the real listener callback/competing-bind negative, genuine signal and cleanup, owned reader/worker joins, instance-root checks and restart. No replacement middleware, private control, reserve/free/rebind, handler replacement, Git/path fork, skip, retry or timeout extension.\", \"rule\": \"RULE-GATE\", \"severity\": \"BLOCKING\", \"status\": \"OPEN\"}, \"reviewer\": \"arch-qa\"}, {\"finding\": {\"category\": \"tests\", \"evidence\": \"Independently hashed both released archives and testing.rs: public instrument_router exists in0.1.1 and is absent in0.2.0. Exact08f7 hosted Linux128252863421/macOS128252863295 fail E0425 at readiness_tests.rs40, runtime_lifecycle.rs106 and owned_runtime.rs46; Windows128252863375 fails at the two portable callsites. All exit101. Raw logs and hashes: rustqa-current-ci-failures.json. This establishes a qualification incompatibility; no production runtime defect is alleged.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests.rs\", \"id\": \"C2-REQ-009\", \"issue\": \"Required causal canceled-readiness/runtime-ownership tests do not compile against the actual pinned published SDK0.2.0. The genuine public timeout/tracking helper is absent, so instance-lock retention through real cleanup and portable canceled-readiness ownership are not currently qualified.\", \"line\": 40, \"recommendation\": \"Have the upstream owner publish the compatible optional public timeout/tracking wrapper, consume that approved release coherently, and qualify the preserved real middleware, cleanup, signals, actual joins and lock/restart controls within all original budgets. Do not delete tests, replace middleware, use private controls or widen deadlines.\", \"severity\": \"critical\"}, \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\"}], \"scope\": \"Preserve occurrence-specific source corrections and actual platform limits; final sole-enforcer report pending publication.\", \"screen\": \"all_not_applicable; no waiver or suppression\", \"severity\": \"Blocking\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

